               <head>Barāhīn-i qāṭiʻ by Kamāl al-Dīn ibn Fakhr al-Dīn Jahrumī</head>
               <msContents>
                  <summary>Chapters nine and ten of a Persian translation of the Arabic <title
                        xml:lang="ar-Latn-x-lc" key="work_600">al-Ṣawāʿiq al-muḥriqah</title> by
                        <persName xml:lang="ar-Latn-x-lc" key="person_100387532">Ibn Ḥajar
                        al-Haythamī</persName> completed in 994/1568 and dedicated to Ibrāhīm ʻĀdil
                     Shāh II (r. 1580–1627).</summary>
                  <msItem class="https://lccn.loc.gov/sh2009127610 https://lccn.loc.gov/sh85121390"
                     n="1" xml:id="Uk_Delhi_Persian_263B-item1">
                     <textLang mainLang="fa" otherLangs="ar">Persian and Arabic</textLang>
                     <note>
                        <p>Dated colophon (f. 135v): completed at the dār al-mulk <placeName>Bāns
                              Barīlī</placeName>( <placeName>Bans Bareilly</placeName>, Uttar
                           Pradesh), Jumādá al-Avval 1244/November-December 1828. </p>
                        <p>Nastaʿlīq.</p>
                        <p>Annotations and corrections in margins.</p>
                        <p>Stamped foliation.</p>
                        <p>Lacking original covers.</p>
                        <p>Deep brown blind-tooled leather binging, gilded only along the spine.</p>
                        <p>Folios cropped; wormholes.</p>
                        <p>IOL Microfilm 478.</p>
                     </note>
                     <title xml:lang="fa-Latn-x-lc" key="work_23854">Barāhīn-i qāṭiʻ</title>
                     <title xml:lang="fa">براهین قاطع</title>
                     <author>
                        <persName xml:lang="fa-Latn-x-lc" key="person_f9005">Kamāl al-Dīn ibn Fakhr al-Dīn
                           Jahrumī</persName>
                        <persName xml:lang="fa">كمال الدين ابن فخر الدين جهرمي</persName>
                     </author>
                  </msItem>
               </msContents>
